WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.742
Human heart anatomy observes the heart divided into two distinct and separated partitions;

00:00:06.792 --> 00:00:11.950
a deoxygenated, or low-oxygen partition, and an oxygenated partition.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.454
There are some human congenital heart conditions that

00:00:15.504 --> 00:00:19.950
can result in this oxygenated and deoxygenated blood mixing, however.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.579
More on that at the end. Arteries generally carry blood “away” from the heart.

00:00:25.629 --> 00:00:26.950
Think “A” for away.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.028
Arteries are typically oxygen-rich but there are exceptions.

00:00:31.078 --> 00:00:33.950
Veins generally carry blood “to” the heart.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.950
Veins typically are oxygen-poor but there are exceptions.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.507
Capillaries are small blood vessels and it is at the capillary level where oxygen is delivered to

00:00:43.557 --> 00:00:48.950
organs and tissues and where carbon dioxide will also be picked up to travel back to the lungs.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.592
So, looking at this heart, the right side (and that’s the person’s right,

00:00:53.642 --> 00:00:59.950
so for you it will look opposite) pumps deoxygenated blood and the left side pumps oxygenated blood.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.785
We can also see 4 chambers:

00:01:01.835 --> 00:01:06.950
the right atrium and right ventricle and the left atrium and left ventricle.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.370
I like to remember that A comes before V in the alphabet so that

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.950
helps me remember the A’s – for atria- are at the top of the heart.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.959
V for ventricles- are at the bottom of the heart.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:20.950
Atria also have thinner walls than the thicker walled ventricles.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.950
The heart also contains valves which we’ll see when we get to tracing the pathway of blood.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.246
The valves are one-way structures that help separate

00:01:29.296 --> 00:01:32.288
the chambers and also prevent backflow of blood.

00:01:32.338 --> 00:01:34.950
Ready to take the adventure of a lifetime?
